Title: Worktree GC must never touch active sessions — rails in the script, GC stays in molt
Created: 2026-07-14
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-07-14T21:40Z claude created
2026-07-14T22:30Z claude note author refined the ruling: molt (housekeeping) keeps GC but must never touch active sessions; roar only disposes of its own merged worktree; rails moved into worktree-gc.sh itself

--- body ---
## Context
On 2026-07-13 the worktree GC (`scripts/worktree-gc.sh`) removed two
worktrees that were live sessions' base cwds:

- 09:15Z — a roar wrap-up removed `explore-session` while four sessions
  were active in it.
- 19:35Z — a roar in `t-gaze-fork-liveness` removed
  `explore-ticket-pipeline` while one session was mid-flight and two more
  had started in it two minutes earlier.

The GC's staleness test (upstream `[gone]` + clean tree) reads "branch
merged" as "worktree unused". A session-base worktree whose checked-out
branch was pushed and merged (PRs #554/#555 merged from
`worktree-explore-ticket-pipeline`; deleteBranchOnMerge pruned the remote)
becomes GC-bait while sessions still sit in it. Removal strands them in
unregistered husk dirs where git resolves to the primary checkout —
roughly eight sessions ran unisolated in the `explore-ticket-pipeline`
husk over the following two days.

Author ruling (refined 2026-07-14): housekeeping (/molt) owns worktree GC,
but it must never touch an active session's worktree; roar exits and
disposes of its OWN merged worktree only, no repo-wide sweep. The
active-session protection lives in the script, not in skill prose:

- **Liveness rail** — skip any removal candidate that is a live process's
  cwd (`/proc/*/cwd` scan; the claude CLI holds its cwd at the session
  base for the session's life). This is the "live base cwd" signal ticket
  0338 called the hard part.
- **Lock rail** — a locked worktree is skipped, never unlock-and-removed.
  The previous unlock-first behavior defeated the very marker molt's
  step-0 active-session guard treats as "in use".

## Relevant files
- `scripts/worktree-gc.sh` — liveness + lock rails; checked past the
  `[gone]` gate so a quiet repo stays silent
- `skills/molt/SKILL.md` — step 1.5 GC retained, documents the rails
- `skills/roar/SKILL.md` — repo-wide GC step removed; step 9 (exit and
  dispose own worktree) unchanged
- `skills/lair/SKILL.md` — defers GC to molt (step 1); keeps
  `git worktree prune` and the orphaned-WIP caveat
- `tests/test_worktree_tools.py` — locked test flipped to skip;
  live-process-cwd skip test added

## Exit criteria
- [ ] roar SKILL.md no longer invokes `worktree-gc.sh`
- [ ] molt SKILL.md keeps the GC step and documents the rails
- [ ] `worktree-gc.sh` skips live-process-cwd and locked worktrees
- [ ] Tests prove both rails (locked skip, live-cwd skip)
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Residual (not this ticket)
The `explore-ticket-pipeline` husk still hosts live sessions and needs
repair once they end. Husk removal policy stays report-only (tickets
0325/0338).
